Data licence
============

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the source code of this project. It does not
cover the map data, which comes from OpenStreetMap and carries its own terms.

    Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
    Licence (ODbL) v1.0.

    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
    https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/


What this covers
----------------

Any file in this repository derived from OpenStreetMap, which currently means:

    pipeline/fixtures/mini/buildings.geojson    building footprints and tags
    pipeline/fixtures/mini/graph.graphml        pedestrian street network

and, once the pipeline emits them, every built city artifact under
web/static/data/ (the street graph, the building footprints and heights, and
anything computed from them).

The pipeline downloads from OpenStreetMap and reshapes what it downloads, so
its output is a derived database in the ODbL's sense. That is why the licence
travels with the data even though the code that produced it is MIT.


What that means if you use this
-------------------------------

Attribute. Any public use of the data, including a deployed copy of the web
client, must credit "© OpenStreetMap contributors" somewhere a user can see.

Share alike. If you publish a modified version of the data, publish it under
the ODbL as well. This obligation is on the data, not on your code: you may
keep your own source code under any licence you like, MIT included.

Nothing here restricts the code. Fork it, change it, sell it, relicense your
changes. The only obligations attach to the map data, and they come from
OpenStreetMap rather than from this project.
